

                          Xcel-Edit Version .105
                            coded by J Vasher
                              Mar 4, 1992

v.97 Changes:
   Bug fixed with a couple of display problems with menu's not clearing.
   bug fixed with Pulling up text when backspace or Delete key used on lines
   greater then term height.

v.98
   Spell checker added.
   Importer added for adding text to your dictionary. You must run this
   after you append your text to the dictionary and sort it with the dos
   sort routine. This program creates and sets up the SIndex file which goes
   in the data directory. You Must be in the data directory with the 
	dictionary, to run this program.

	Get File and Put File added you must have maintence access to use. 

v.99
	Bug fixed with detecting 80 column vt100 would lock... 
	couple of minor bug fixes with the __saveds.
	Auto sets stack size 8196....

v.100
	Bug with importing text causing formating to go weird. (this is a hack) to
	fix a problem with the way the bbs handles the edit buffer.
	Bug with leaving editor messing up display fixed.
	Bug fix when user didnt' support vt100 or 80 didn't exit properly causing 
   recoverable alert.
	bug when moving text around using CTRL O options. Would not redisplay and
	lose lines.

v.102
	Remove some pesky as well as anoyiing enforcer hits.

v.103
	Add the CTRL W feature to do BBS commands, and allow remote sysops to do
	directorys from within the editor.

v.104
	Fixed major bug on security.  Thanks to The Trooper. Please don't word 
	about this bug, unless you can spread this program.
	Enforcer hit on exit, when users didn't have vt100 or 80 columns.

v.105
	Recompile for new headers....

Warning:
	There is future plans to move Vised to an Editor directory, when this 
	Occurs there should be no problems moving vised. However, keep a watch
   for this to occur.

To Install:
   You should have the following files:
                                     
      o Editor.Help               > Text/Editor.Help
      o Addtext1741       add to  > languages/english
      o Vised000  030             > data/vised OR Editor/VisEd
      o Importer                  > c:Importer
      o dictionary                > Ram:dictionary or data/dictionary
      o sindex                    > data/sindex

   You need to copy the appropriate VisedXXX to your data directory, rename
it as "VISED". Then copy Editor.Help to your TEXT directory, and finally, 
add the textfile ADDTEXT1741 to line 1741 and on of languages/BBStext
Replacing existing Vised text. ReBOOT or rerun master and you should be 
all set.

	Please use caution when adding text, only the lines that exist in the 
file should be added.

   I have put many hours into Xcel_Edit, and have just finished a total 
rewrite of the program from scratch. Here are some of the features of the
Editor:

                  o Shift cursor keys beg end of line top bot of buffer.
                  o Fully functional point and click local interface.
                    for all commands on the menu lines.
                  o Highlight lines, and select options with mouse.
                  o Redraw for both current line and entire screen.
                  o Spell checker.
                  o Put and Get files (Sysop only!)
                  o View function allow you to test text files for
                    proper display (IPL)
                  o Quick Save feature.
                  o 28 control commands.
                  o Cursor controlled editing.
                  o Help screen.
                  o Search & Replace.
                  o Block move, copy, and kill options.
                  o Status line toggle for slower bauds.
   
   Currently there is a few known bugs, one has to do with the Excelsior 
Imports text, for some odd reason, I end up with lines longer then 80 chars.
In order to deal with these until hopefully the import improves, I simply chop
the lines off, This is noticeable when editing IBM files I think it has
something to do with CTRL M and CTRL J both being used. Tabs are expanded to
Seven spaces. Unless someone has a better suggestion, this works....

   This version has many major bug fixes over the 73d version which was the
last release. Some that even amazed me how the system functioned. Hopefully
All bugs are history, but I know better please report any problems, like
or dislike. Or just drop a note saying HI! 

